think Crux-first among the three siblings. morphology already carries dilate_h/_v + erode_h/_v single-axis passes, so an axis-aligned directional element and a wider composed radius are thin compositions of what stands -- low crux. The decisive generalization that opens the directional element, the cross, the disk, AND the hit-or-miss transform all at once is a GENERAL structuring element: dilate/erode over an arbitrary bounded offset set. That is the Lindy-first crux -- the floor many shapes descend from -- and it mirrors the convolve -> convolve_n general-contains-special pattern the family already loves.
think Grepped image/ -- no structuring-element module (the three matches were compose, font5x7_upper_close, glyph_compose, unrelated). A clean gap.
think Built image/structure.rye in the morphology idiom: an Offset {dx,dy:i32}, a StructuringElement {offsets:[]const Offset}, one comptime-is_max apply() gathering max/min over the offset set (each axis clamped at the border), dilate_se/erode_se, a guard refusing EmptySource/EmptyElement/StructureElementTooLarge by name before any allocation, bounded by structure_max_offsets (65536, a 256x256 ceiling). Both verbs read the same offset set at p+offset -- the symmetric-element convention the square floor uses, under which the duality holds for a center-symmetric element.
think Witness tools/structure_witness.rish in the family shape. GREEN on the first full metal run, no reds: the GENERAL-CONTAINS-SPECIAL crux (a square offset set == morphology.dilate/erode byte-for-byte at radius 1 and 2 on a colored translucent field); a CROSS grows a dot into a plus and leaves the diagonals black where a square would light them (the shape matters); a directional LINE widens a vertical line horizontally yet leaves every column whole; the DUALITY law for the symmetric cross; a single-offset element the identity for both verbs; alpha morphed; QOI round-trip byte-for-byte; three refusals by name; determinism.
obs Crux-first over count-padding: opening the general floor (which makes the hit-or-miss transform a natural next sibling) beats taking the two easy siblings the existing single-axis passes already nearly cover. The general contains the special, so nothing the square path proved is lost -- the witness proves that equality directly rather than asserting it.
obs Same-set convention named honestly in the doc: erode and dilate gather the same offset set (p+offset), so the duality is proven for a symmetric element (the cross); an asymmetric element's classical reflected-erosion duality is out of this rung's scope, stated rather than overclaimed.
